<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37265" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Postŭmus</span></b> ,
		i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a Roman surname.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> M. Curtius Postumus, <i>a friend of Cicero</i>, <i>and the
				accuser of Murena</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Fam. 13, 5, 2 sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> C. Rabirius Postumus, <i>defended by
				Cicero</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Rab. Post. 1, 1</span></i>
			sqq.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			Ursidius Postumus, <i>to whom is addressed the sixth
				satire of Juvenal</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 6, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">377</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
